nsus leans Democratic and markets price Rutinel near 85%, while the lone poll shows only a two-point Evans edge. Evans's cash advantage and incumbency keep this short of Likely D.", "watch": "Any late independent polling or a shift in the spending balance could move this toward Tossup if Evans closes the air-war gap.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Gabe Evans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Colorado's 8th District is among the tightest House races in the country, a seat decided by less than a point in each of the last two cycles. First-term Republican Gabe Evans faces Democrat Manny Rutinel in a rematch-style contest that has featured sharp debates and heavy outside spending. Trump's unpopularity in Colorado is a headwind for Evans, and most expert raters now place the race at Lean D or Tossup, with several expecting a flip.\n\nRutinel benefits from roughly $3.5 million in outside support against modest Republican outside spending, though Evans holds a large cash-on-hand advantage. The only public poll, from a Republican-leaning pollster in mid-September, showed Evans up two. Prediction markets price Rutinel's chances around 83 to 85 percent, making this a modest Democratic edge rather than a true tossup.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7652, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7649, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7806, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7027, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6862, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7621, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7968, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7638, "margin": 4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.6}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8011, "margin": 4.6}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8034, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-1